675230" "q-127736/selection/81048e996037ec00ebd726d167ee0e4dea99dbed7e0902b4c74051f50a81a729" "q-127736/selection/0a39b98f8bc8c43c345a4bae7e8d899031d3abc4e6d432eb59023f3e4a934d9e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-127736" :question/id #uuid "9fd0e8ab-5ed1-5462-b099-07b3173547c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-127736" :question/problem "Calculate ${Z}^{-1}$ where\n$Z=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 8\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Given a $2\\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\nZ=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe inverse of $Z$ can be found using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Z}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(Z)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the determinant:\n\n$$\ndet(Z)=1\\cdot 8-3\\cdot 2=2\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, then, the inverse is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Z}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(Z)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}8 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can verify the result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Z{Z}^{-1} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}8 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓ \\\\ {Z}^{-1}Z & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}8 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-127736/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bea23649-e835-540a-b238-7b89ed330cd3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-127736"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-127744/selection/646971a055ed277c2082c44a11d64801b7070b155fcb13bc3a1fa5c7ac53d052" :answer/id #uuid "f136e859-7d84-5d24-a3cc-1fb3c7e2a042" :answe