ix\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe inverse of $A$ can be found using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the determinant:\n\n$$\ndet(A)=6\\cdot 1-2\\cdot 9=-12\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, then, the inverse is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-12}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -9 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1/12 & 1/6 \\\\ 3/4 & -1/2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can verify the result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{A}^{-1} & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 2 \\\\ 9 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1/12 & 1/6 \\\\ 3/4 & -1/2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓ \\\\ {A}^{-1}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-1/12 & 1/6 \\\\ 3/4 & -1/2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}6 & 2 \\\\ 9 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-316780/field-1" "q-316780/field-2" "q-316780/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bea23649-e835-540a-b238-7b89ed330cd3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316780"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-127742/selection/973d5da40ea4a35293f1fc6fb0f727b5444dbaf531d8a28250592c4f4f650176" :answer/id #uuid "7c794efe-e4d2-5478-8cef-b8f0335411da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127742/selection/a6c72afe7cf055ac049067a9d05c2dbc749986db14fb09dd0b390cdce627a44c" :answer/id #uuid "8dd9b462-c5f5-514f-bd5e-cd2427a802cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127742/selection/305753be6cd2db1357d18b2d713b723217e226906ea6881890e7d69e756532ae" :answer/id #uuid "9b0e4e4f-019b-54ff-a8b6-17c2dfffcb34" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127742/selection/7cd747283b2158ae893992d764d184fc54f9d8233306dcf1aa1f02fec5c55e70" :answer/id #uuid "3a853d67-92d5-535e-b468-8e02dad2a667" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127742/selection/3691fd16acf6fbd3a61bbc1d619b3fdd1aaef53f19ba9f0a57ea993eee533ae9" :answer/id #uuid "8867e674-61b8-52d5-8b4f-392b6107371a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127742/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "11f04062-ea30-5d75-a3e3-2839fb18deea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-127742/selection/973d5da40ea4a35293f1fc6fb0f727b5444dbaf531d8a28250592c4f4f650176" :answer-field/choices ["q-127742/selection/973d5da40ea4a35293f1fc6fb0f727b5444dbaf531d8a28250592c4f4f650176" "q-127742/selection/a6c72afe7cf055ac049067a9d05c2dbc749986db14fb09dd0b390cdce627a44c" "q-127742/selection/305753be6cd2db1357d18b2d713b723217e226906ea6881890e7d69e756532ae" "q-127742/selection/7cd747283b2158ae893992d764d184fc54f9d8233306dcf1aa1f02fec5c55e70" "q-127742/selection/3691fd16acf6fbd3a61bbc1d619b3fdd1aaef53f19ba9f0a57ea993eee533ae9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-127742" :question/id #uuid "469cce88-f2bf-5c3e-aa47-9c15a4251782" :question/math-academy-id "q-127742" :question/problem "Calculate ${B}^{-1}$, where \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Given a $2\\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe inverse of $B$ can be found using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{B}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(B)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the determinant:\n\n$$\ndet(B)=2\\cdot 0-1\\cdot 1=-1\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, then, the inverse is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{B}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(B)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-1)}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can verify the result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B{B}^{-1} & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓ \\\\ {B}^{-1}B & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-127742/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bea23649-e835-540a-b238-7b89ed330cd3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-127742"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-11717/selection/b5a6da364b287006e34b182b58dfa854402f8e2dbf84907513d8f72251dce705" :answer/id #uuid "66eb4339-b5c8-5b6f-a9c6-736fc2c5a548" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$H$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11717/selection/efdaf8f058ed7f69696fe27bb51424678e17e71ffdf76d16afdf9b0858aef2c2" :answer/id #uuid "bc62ee22-7c25-5746-b95d-31e50a024745" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$J$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11717/selection/72ac95e265b43c4993705cf48fb60b35231009ecd2db7aaf18656abdc84cd043" :answer/id #uuid "d0033e22-6e20-53c9-b6ad-5502fdbe9286" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$H$ and $J$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11717/selection/504992b1a8dcdd6b33c06eb09f2c115769320e41afefcb669d71f93bba6b8fd9" :answer/id #uuid "a7780f8d-92ee-5bee-acda-ac38b221ba98" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$J$ and $K$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11717/selection/36c8585ee7c2c30d5375b8a3f706f0ef62e6c56469fb099c00096526399ac975" :answer/id #uuid "2dd25a02-4e2e-592b-b869-2889bf56d0f5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$H$ and $K$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11717/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5e00ec5e-d2cb-5618-b9fc-572db656a6be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-11717/selection/72ac95e265b43c4993705cf48fb60b35231009ecd2db7aaf18656abdc84cd043" :answer-field/choices ["q-11717/selection/b5a6da364b287006e34b182b58dfa854402f8e2dbf84907513d8f72251dce705" "q-11717/selection/efdaf8f058ed7f69696fe27bb51424678e17e71ffdf76d16afdf9b0858aef2c2" "q-11717/selection/72ac95e265b43c4993705cf48fb60b35231009ecd2db7aaf18656abdc84cd043" "q-11717/selection/504992b1a8dcdd6b33c06eb09f2c115769320e41afefcb669d71f93bba6b8fd9" "q-11717/selection/36c8585ee7c2c30d5375b8a3f706f0ef62e6c56469fb099c00096526399ac975"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-11717" :question/id #uuid "1b4d40e2-069c-5e10-923d-ef1e82d45a9d" :question/math-academy-id "q-11717" :question/problem "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\n$$\nH=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,J=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{aligned}],\\,K=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "- For the matrix $H$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(H)=5\\cdot 0-3\\cdot 0=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(H)=0,$ we conclude that $H$ is not invertible. Since $H$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $H$ is singular.\n\n- For the matrix $J$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(J)=2\\cdot 6-3\\cdot 4=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(J)=0,$ we conclude that $J$ is not invertible. Since $J$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $J$ is singular.\n\n- The matrix $K$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. So, it is not invertible. Since the matrix is not square, we can't say that it's singular.\n\nTherefore, only $H$ and $J$ is singular." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-11717/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c6056ee-15f3-5b5c-8a14-173ea1da1381"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-11717"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-127755/selection/e432f1020975ada4c83798ae75bfd6c0ae4dfe63215763f08b8be8ccabf8a5d3" :answer/id #uuid "0ab1e606-956f-5e6a-9469-fed13fe02408" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127755/selection/685c02320dbe687345f93d820499dea4c0c82808b910e8a0e5841f77aa82209d" :answer/id #uuid "80a494ed-44d2-5724-9640-8d14f9568a20" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127755/selection/b967c3002b3f913c5b31990d1f8159d3e1e979aa07e2842a8b67bfff1a2fd3f2" :answer/id #uuid "10f774ec-34c7-5491-b105-7e351e4551a5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127755/selection/2377e3ffc3b5cd65e1036103e0b988e5af6634b2438c63c3b7cc0592571401ab" :answer/id #uuid "4ba5decc-4f40-528a-a242-a3d3e92808a2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127755/selection/e956c3af673c94782038951d8de50bf89c9a53bf4daf2ca6725a4bea4229074c" :answer/id #uuid "318c1cb7-b02b-5fd4-86c9-3bba63f9bdc6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127755/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2776ffed-7e53-5e1b-9126-769874216821" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-127755/selection/2377e3ffc3b5cd65e1036103e0b988e5af6634b2438c63c3b7cc0592571401ab" :answer-field/choices ["q-127755/selection/e432f1020975ada4c83798ae75bfd6c0ae4dfe63215763f08b8be8ccabf8a5d3" "q-127755/selection/685c02320dbe687345f93d820499dea4c0c82808b910e8a0e5841f77aa82209d" "q-127755/selection/b967c3002b3f913c5b31990d1f8159d3e1e979aa07e2842a8b67bfff1a2fd3f2" "q-127755/selection/2377e3ffc3b5cd65e1036103e0b988e5af6634b2438c63c3b7cc0592571401ab" "q-127755/selection/e956c3af673c94782038951d8de50bf89c9a53bf4daf2ca6725a4bea4229074c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-127755" :question/id #uuid "cb5cfafe-438d-561a-bfca-e1cc33842ff2" :question/math-academy-id "q-127755" :question/problem "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "- The matrix $A$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix. So, it is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $B$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(B)=0\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot 1=1.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(B)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $B$ is invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $C$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(C)=1\\cdot 2-2\\cdot 1=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(C)=0,$ we conclude that $C$ is not invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $C$ do not have an inverse." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-127755/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c6056ee-15f3-5b5c-8a14-173ea1da1381"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-127755"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-127757/selection/c2d0c654ca5e5a48392b15549a3a4470b39e6aaa299393dbe95e6c716da431aa" :answer/id #uuid "231b50e7-c515-5b7a-8237-1688f362c11c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$S$ and $U$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127757/selection/16b50194516e7dcad35bdecafc4c70a67642e9c995267daaf0accfcc873be095" :answer/id #uuid "98ca54b2-8431-5444-9efe-fdbd7d2615eb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$U$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127757/selection/5572e02e27f0cbc239ccd93fb0f30c843c05a3432e80728a1f2acd6bf56149c0" :answer/id #uuid "46e22156-77f8-53ae-b232-4c1481123bd5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$S$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127757/selection/27ead39b22315899a97d19d41807fad901038aea957324f0c89ba36f126544db" :answer/id #uuid "142c305f-1241-5ca4-bd3c-20f1cc8d1f80" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$T$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127757/selection/5ef8b91ab792fb70e6e33cb21719b226bf2e45754b4c703f44085d2c4d3959c0" :answer/id #uuid "2c91a010-1966-513a-b4c0-a950a36e14de" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$T$ and $S$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127757/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f9614a24-643b-5a1c-a444-f3d4704932cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-127757/selection/27ead39b22315899a97d19d41807fad901038aea957324f0c89ba36f126544db" :answer-field/choices ["q-127757/selection/c2d0c654ca5e5a48392b15549a3a4470b39e6aaa299393dbe95e6c716da431aa" "q-127757/selection/16b50194516e7dcad35bdecafc4c70a67642e9c995267daaf0accfcc873be095" "q-127757/selection/5572e02e27f0cbc239ccd93fb0f30c843c05a3432e80728a1f2acd6bf56149c0" "q-127757/selection/27ead39b22315899a97d19d41807fad901038aea957324f0c89ba36f126544db" "q-127757/selection/5ef8b91ab792fb70e6e33cb21719b226bf2e45754b4c703f44085d2c4d3959c0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-127757" :question/id #uuid "4a2fb10f-1cf2-5a6b-8b70-3549d9280b9f" :question/math-academy-id "q-127757" :question/problem "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\n$$\nS=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,T=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -6\\end{aligned}],\\,U=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "- For the matrix $S$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(S)=1\\cdot (-1)-(-1)\\cdot 0=-1.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(S)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $S$ is invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $T$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(T)=2\\cdot (-6)-4\\cdot (-3)=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(T)=0,$ we conclude that $T$ is not invertible. Since $T$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $T$ is singular.\n\n- For the matrix $U$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(U)=0\\cdot 0-1\\cdot (-1)=1.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(U)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $U$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $T$ is singular." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-127757/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c6056ee-15f3-5b5c-8a14-173ea1da1381"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-127757"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-7915/selection/5f6c142a82c4a0bf971b412708f6830f8e50a71860d9c4cebbd361a473710cf0" :answer/id #uuid "22d4b04f-11f1-54a1-b303-31bafb35f4af" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$Q$ and $R$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7915/selection/2e147b9bf74fe5a9fe1cc06d49c56b8c05578bddb93b65358c386cfaa2e4aa36" :answer/id #uuid "15691103-f36a-5181-b7a7-283236c096ea" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$P$ and $R$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7915/selection/afe4b97c823938f24ee0f462e6dae1ce1a6e74074abfb6f3f9af3b253499f0cc" :answer/id #uuid "81a41221-0341-56ab-9673-afb161d21f94" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$Q$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7915/selection/f6ed8c3e8ac11c4c476e856e67261d9addd41c460d2f0404e6d3f3a72ad0633a" :answer/id #uuid "b5da8682-de33-580e-bb9b-32f89484ae5f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$P$ and $Q$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7915/selection/be5beffd9a95134974e6bda496907ef99198947107984fe7477f4a7dcf5134a9" :answer/id #uuid "3952685f-e03a-542f-a8e8-f37ba5a3c54a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$P$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7915/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "074b9c92-0e09-5b09-a3cf-2efb2a6798f7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-7915/selection/f6ed8c3e8ac11c4c476e856e67261d9addd41c460d2f0404e6d3f3a72ad0633a" :answer-field/choices ["q-7915/selection/5f6c142a82c4a0bf971b412708f6830f8e50a71860d9c4cebbd361a473710cf0" "q-7915/selection/2e147b9bf74fe5a9fe1cc06d49c56b8c05578bddb93b65358c386cfaa2e4aa36" "q-7915/selection/afe4b97c823938f24ee0f462e6dae1ce1a6e74074abfb6f3f9af3b253499f0cc" "q-7915/selection/f6ed8c3e8ac11c4c476e856e67261d9addd41c460d2f0404e6d3f3a72ad0633a" "q-7915/selection/be5beffd9a95134974e6bda496907ef99198947107984fe7477f4a7dcf5134a9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-7915" :question/id #uuid "17761662-c8e1-5053-be1d-f17ca1632a52" :question/math-academy-id "q-7915" :question/problem "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 8 & 6\\end{aligned}],\\,Q=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,R=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "- For the matrix $P$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(P)=4\\cdot 6-8\\cdot 3=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(P)=0,$ we conclude that $P$ is not invertible. Since $P$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $P$ is singular.\n\n- For the matrix $Q$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(Q)=1\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot (-1)=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(Q)=0,$ we conclude that $Q$ is not invertible. Since $Q$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $Q$ is singular.\n\n- The matrix $R$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix. So, it is not invertible. Since the matrix is not square, we can't say that it's singular.\n\nTherefore, only $P$ and $Q$ are singular." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-7915/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c6056ee-15f3-5b5c-8a14-173ea1da1381"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-7915"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-71938/selection/2e692c2c22b13ad5cb6847ef7d1b323a5f743cdf1942762db62d61728ef40842" :answer/id #uuid "08eb2ea7-f792-5e17-ba62-6cb93b9a1555" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$X$ and $Z$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71938/selection/5e9f66473e935286c2c56e5c56d0e9bef280993c627d4fc6831375267448e72b" :answer/id #uuid "3e2c51de-d9e4-53e2-8df8-7c5a5dda12ce" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$Y$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71938/selection/e9fd4ecbf5bd4e38cdf04eddf835d10f6558fdeb7d74633d2e2ec15764de2bc2" :answer/id #uuid "c5ed6083-9a87-5d3f-8c78-32388cdb4327" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$X$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71938/selection/9271c1026b9fd2e189ef39350f9a41159873b5bc0ead6717e38e78c613348fc6" :answer/id #uuid "d7884f22-d342-599e-b966-702453ae8925" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$Z$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71938/selection/5920de69bad89e985e4e53d383add0ef7ed3bd9785fc97e11b12a0257746e67f" :answer/id #uuid "6b708952-cde1-539c-b2ec-210459186665" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$X$ and $Y$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71938/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bd54c950-30a6-5bde-8785-a5144115b030" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-71938/selection/e9fd4ecbf5bd4e38cdf04eddf835d10f6558fdeb7d74633d2e2ec15764de2bc2" :answer-field/choices ["q-71938/selection/2e692c2c22b13ad5cb6847ef7d1b323a5f743cdf1942762db62d61728ef40842" "q-71938/selection/5e9f66473e935286c2c56e5c56d0e9bef280993c627d4fc6831375267448e72b" "q-71938/selection/e9fd4ecbf5bd4e38cdf04eddf835d10f6558fdeb7d74633d2e2ec15764de2bc2" "q-71938/selection/9271c1026b9fd2e189ef39350f9a41159873b5bc0ead6717e38e78c613348fc6" "q-71938/selection/5920de69bad89e985e4e53d383add0ef7ed3bd9785fc97e11b12a0257746e67f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-71938" :question/id #uuid "f34f6a84-b6d1-59f1-84c8-b1742c3a5c7a" :question/math-academy-id "q-71938" :question/problem "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 6 \\\\ 10 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,Y=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{aligned}],\\,Z=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 10 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "- The matrix $X$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. So, it is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $Y$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(Y)=6\\cdot 6-7\\cdot 5=1.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(Y)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $Y$ is invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $Z$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(Z)=(-2)\\cdot 5-10\\cdot 1=-20.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(Z)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $Z$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $X$ does not have an inverse." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-71938/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c6056ee-15f3-5b5c-8a14-173ea1da1381"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71938"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-71969/selection/2a7c1a99e9e23adaa901d3875aa3d18803784074d59c1f3334ed37864b04f786" :answer/id #uuid "7a2432f1-06ef-596e-a4ad-a7b950fab294" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71969/selection/44855ba0613121a1ddbb17cff307d99cb533fdec60ddec9161b81ae8332a6ab0" :answer/id #uuid "d2c77e6d-18f5-5b5d-8323-5394b92b24e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71969/selection/e81adf74c4db6a0bf59a64d0b8573c2fc89a85ac940cc03b1c176c21425e0769" :answer/id #uuid "019324c7-81c8-5b53-bf56-b700abdaa7c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71969/selection/a8fa7792c7b65e1b52cac888c884be5a67307f2982c5e14a5a35ab5c77686dc0" :answer/id #uuid "f965bb0f-74c0-548e-b2a8-2b56e74fca3d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71969/selection/faf4db69034ea0ac5d82f041b78471977a3a98218cbfa67656c051365169fa81" :answer/id #uuid "105cab17-a1b0-5700-a8de-e49a40cb8f6c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71969/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d6d60900-5445-5716-b671-a3f6295914cc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-71969/selection/2a7c1a99e9e23adaa901d3875aa3d18803784074d59c1f3334ed37864b04f786" :answer-field/choices ["q-71969/selection/2a7c1a99e9e23adaa901d3875aa3d18803784074d59c1f3334ed37864b04f786" "q-71969/selection/44855ba0613121a1ddbb17cff307d99cb533fdec60ddec9161b81ae8332a6ab0" "q-71969/selection/e81adf74c4db6a0bf59a64d0b8573c2fc89a85ac940cc03b1c176c21425e0769" "q-71969/selection/a8fa7792c7b65e1b52cac888c884be5a67307f2982c5e14a5a35ab5c77686dc0" "q-71969/selection/faf4db69034ea0ac5d82f041b78471977a3a98218cbfa67656c051365169fa81"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-71969" :question/id #uuid "02eff272-95c3-5a34-a191-db8af4578dbd" :question/math-academy-id "q-71969" :question/problem "If $M=[\\begin{aligned}t & 4 \\\\ t & 10\\end{aligned}]$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value of $t.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $M$ is singular if and only if $det(M)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =t\\cdot 10-t\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =10t-4t \\\\  & =6t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6t & =0 \\\\ t & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $t$ is $t=0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-71969/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e64e0c3-f8f5-5c38-ae75-1aed92e0ac01"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71969"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-316781/field-1/9e11fa4df3725c69efaf2fb0a82d90e47a4519d002f721e23606c3d6290fb02c" :answer/id #uuid "197273cb-fad0-550e-847c-37b81ec3acbd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316781/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "90f007b8-4c17-5edb-8319-70889d75f9bc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316781/field-1/9e11fa4df3725c69efaf2fb0a82d90e47a4519d002f721e23606c3d6290fb02c" :answer-field/choices ["q-316781/field-1/9e11fa4df3725c69efaf2fb0a82d90e47a4519d002f721e23606c3d6290fb02c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316781" :question/id #uuid "332a826c-7348-5345-899f-11bdcbd79a2d" :question/math-academy-id "q-316781" :question/problem "If $B=[\\begin{aligned}2x & 5x-1 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{aligned}]$\nis a singular matrix, calculate the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $B$ is singular if and only if $det(B)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =(2x)\\cdot (-2)-4\\cdot (5x-1) \\\\  & =-4x+4-20x \\\\  & =-24x+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-24x+4 & =0 \\\\ 24x & =4 \\\\ x & =\\frac{4}{24} \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-316781/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e64e0c3-f8f5-5c38-ae75-1aed92e0ac01"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316781"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-11719/selection/7161f3140020b0dd4c15ea58a14042b8788c2ceccaa922c051ca801a7112dea6" :answer/id #uuid "3c5f34b8-d55a-5f8e-b013-27cabcaff0f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11719/selection/bddb16fb60275d07c2d2a20d0ff2251caf856d27ab8e69dbd10410685c39553a" :answer/id #uuid "83da0946-6dc3-516e-8d19-168392f39733" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11719/selection/5beba78f8a87858577a68ec948ce872a0e07d8f73daac0ed26589573d2f3fed5" :answer/id #uuid "05dc6303-a43b-529a-a7f1-9f6d34ebdccb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11719/selection/148cbbc022d3eb8f8a0186a5f1837b0a635335e9b82f4bea4e062deb2288e7e6" :answer/id #uuid "64d8056c-aeec-5a1a-9059-5f0e94f09159" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=\\pm 2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11719/selection/7b3fa644f66fa70a2eb72f51b7d5acdcb6e257a1d02bb9b7ea59d29bb589933b" :answer/id #uuid "f7c0fbba-f976-568b-a400-c82dd733eb64" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=\\pm 3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11719/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "970a4e18-384b-538a-b9f2-9f09c076bae6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-11719/selection/7b3fa644f66fa70a2eb72f51b7d5acdcb6e257a1d02bb9b7ea59d29bb589933b" :answer-field/choices ["q-11719/selection/7161f3140020b0dd4c15ea58a14042b8788c2ceccaa922c051ca801a7112dea6" "q-11719/selection/bddb16fb60275d07c2d2a20d0ff2251caf856d27ab8e69dbd10410685c39553a" "q-11719/selection/5beba78f8a87858577a68ec948ce872a0e07d8f73daac0ed26589573d2f3fed5" "q-11719/selection/148cbbc022d3eb8f8a0186a5f1837b0a635335e9b82f4bea4e062deb2288e7e6" "q-11719/selection/7b3fa644f66fa70a2eb72f51b7d5acdcb6e257a1d02bb9b7ea59d29bb589933b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-11719" :question/id #uuid "4918baf6-577a-5ac9-9070-414a1d323782" :question/math-academy-id "q-11719" :question/problem "If $F=[\\begin{aligned}3 & t \\\\ t & 3\\end{aligned}]$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value(s) of $t.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $F$ is singular if and only if $det(F)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(F) & =3\\cdot 3-t\\cdot t \\\\  & =9-{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9-{t}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {t}^{2} & =9 \\\\ t & =\\pm 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the values of $t$ are $t=\\pm 3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-11719/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e64e0c3-f8f5-5c38-ae75-1aed92e0ac01"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-11719"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-71967/selection/f7031104f14fe004994e4fe4b8af3fbe4e65cfa2bff3c7eab1748f5f2092c758" :answer/id #uuid "4a91fe2a-3f08-55a9-b5d9-651a2576707b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71967/selection/bb4e1be02a1ceee34989c85bcc52e58356b4559f2810da5da714fef2710d4eca" :answer/id #uuid "86cdccf0-1511-503b-bc55-3ff9b7747687" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71967/selection/c3deb073f152a478e46392e1f56479f2987a022223419d7f9c369a815039d205" :answer/id #uuid "acad5599-da05-58ce-b28d-7c6e809a37a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71967/selection/96efe327aa5df1953454aa8a0acb24299d8e2e2f538b2a5f40d98e7332b886b7" :answer/id #uuid "8f632f4a-2e06-5819-a78c-9ccbe8bba4c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71967/selection/1e9f29c284d3d4384ce2a5e04c1013d29b18bf826f8ff61e900714021a9e3327" :answer/id #uuid "66eabc9d-f4f9-5412-a665-bb0699a45bf1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71967/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0b072d1b-91b4-5fae-a33a-27613fcc47a3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-71967/selection/96efe327aa5df1953454aa8a0acb24299d8e2e2f538b2a5f40d98e7332b886b7" :answer-field/choices ["q-71967/selection/f7031104f14fe004994e4fe4b8af3fbe4e65cfa2bff3c7eab1748f5f2092c758" "q-71967/selection/bb4e1be02a1ceee34989c85bcc52e58356b4559f2810da5da714fef2710d4eca" "q-71967/selection/c3deb073f152a478e46392e1f56479f2987a022223419d7f9c369a815039d205" "q-71967/selection/96efe327aa5df1953454aa8a0acb24299d8e2e2f538b2a5f40d98e7332b886b7" "q-71967/selection/1e9f29c284d3d4384ce2a5e04c1013d29b18bf826f8ff61e900714021a9e3327"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-71967" :question/id #uuid "b2d15958-4ecb-5c0d-ac09-3fa2b8146b35" :question/math-academy-id "q-71967" :question/problem "If $V=[\\begin{aligned}7 & y \\\\ 5 & y\\end{aligned}]$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value of $y.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $V$ is singular if and only if $det(V)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(V) & =7\\cdot y-5\\cdot y \\\\  & =7y-5y \\\\  & =2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2y & =0 \\\\ y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $y$ is $y=0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-71967/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e64e0c3-f8f5-5c38-ae75-1aed92e0ac01"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71967"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-127905/selection/4e9502384bd1c7eaf828e1454561f3a99074335f900bf9b06d5132879407a76a" :answer/id #uuid "70d152d1-86e9-5140-a55b-3ebeb9302b3e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "n=\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127905/selection/a9cacd8bc2b0d28fb90fa039fd98fe4ba104dd8b5c5a2bed7dc9ed4f82745bfb" :answer/id #uuid "b0b57769-1377-5313-9201-b4ea5d6d89ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "n=10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127905/selection/6e138a7010824783c08c4399f81d5569fd12cec9f7c9af6809852b946d0668fa" :answer/id #uuid "53b2b1b1-a040-515f-8ffa-ebc582ed8323" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "n=\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127905/selection/f2a5d01cfc4f23e1d6ccb529b7a18867711103e45639d5ca3d85d88d365e03dc" :answer/id #uuid "6931d6c5-02bd-5e7c-908e-ef0826835da0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "n=\\pm 8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127905/selection/078aa7f9eec13f8491deb044fe9d29b7baefc8f50bd8f1ac7928ec042b84bd06" :answer/id #uuid "46fe4e6a-5d64-59e8-b59a-19cbcaf729d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "n=\\pm 4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127905/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b3ed19da-636c-5863-a76b-57450e5b6b5a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-127905/selection/f2a5d01cfc4f23e1d6ccb529b7a18867711103e45639d5ca3d85d88d365e03dc" :answer-field/choices ["q-127905/selection/4e9502384bd1c7eaf828e1454561f3a99074335f900bf9b06d5132879407a76a" "q-127905/selection/a9cacd8bc2b0d28fb90fa039fd98fe4ba104dd8b5c5a2bed7dc9ed4f82745bfb" "q-127905/selection/6e138a7010824783c08c4399f81d5569fd12cec9f7c9af6809852b946d0668fa" "q-127905/selection/f2a5d01cfc4f23e1d6ccb529b7a18867711103e45639d5ca3d85d88d365e03dc" "q-127905/selection/078aa7f9eec13f8491deb044fe9d29b7baefc8f50bd8f1ac7928ec042b84bd06"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-127905" :question/id #uuid "901178dd-d45f-581f-a10a-55eab419017e" :question/math-academy-id "q-127905" :question/problem "If $P=[\\begin{aligned}n & -4 \\\\ -16 & n\\end{aligned}]$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value(s) of $n.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $P$ is singular if and only if $det(P)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P) & =n\\cdot n-(-16)\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & ={n}^{2}-64.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $n:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}^{2}-64 & =0 \\\\ {n}^{2} & =64 \\\\ n & =\\pm 8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the values of $n$ are $n=\\pm 8.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-127905/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e64e0c3-f8f5-5c38-ae75-1aed92e0ac01"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-127905"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4502"] :question/problem "Calculate $A^{-1},$ where\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Given a $2 \\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nthe inverse of $A$ can be found using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\det(A) = 1 \\cdot 1 - 0 \\cdot (-2) = 1\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, then, the inverse is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}]. \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -0 \\\\ -(-2) & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can verify the result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{A}^{-1} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓ \\\\ {A}^{-1}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4503"] :question/problem "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "- For the matrix $A$, we have\n\n$$\n\\det({A})=1 \\cdot 1 - 1 \\cdot 1 = 0.\n$$\n\nBecause $\\det(A)=0,$ we conclude that $A$ is not invertible. Since $A$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $A$ is singular.\n\n- The matrix $B$ is a $3 \\times 2$ matrix. So, it is not invertible. Since the matrix is not square, we can't say that it's singular.\n\n- For the matrix $C$, we have\n\n$$\n\\det({C})=3 \\cdot 3 - (-3) \\cdot 3 = 18.\n$$\n\nBecause $\\det(C) \\neq 0,$ we conclude that $C$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $A$ is singular." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4504"] :question/problem "If \n$[\\begin{aligned}1-k & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1-k\\end{aligned}]$\n is a singular matrix, calculate the value(s) of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $A$ is singular if and only if $\\det(A)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =(1-k)(1-k)-4 \\\\  & ={k}^{2}-2k-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $k\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{k}^{2}-2k-3 & =0 \\\\ (k-3)(k+1) & =0 \\\\ k & =3,-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the values of $k$ are $k=3$ and $k=-1.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
